-- title:
--   Cubic call-depth bound for wanted records and shared sources
-- statement:
--   For natural input size $n$, use the scheduled dimensions $h=\operatorname{microHalf}(\operatorname{inputBits}(n))$ and $J=\operatorname{blockCount}(\operatorname{inputBits}(n))$. Let $S=\operatorname{scale}(n)$, the sum of the shared-bank magnitude envelope, local-cover initialization envelope, maximum modulus, prime window, $n$, and $100$.
--   Let $R=\operatorname{radix}(n)$, $g$ be the band width, and $I=g\operatorname{ColorBandBounds.count}(n,g)$ the raw-incidence capacity. The combined wanted-and-source stage has depth budget
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}
--   D(n,R,I)&=\max\{512h+J+\lceil\log_2R\rceil+3I+13,\;512hJ+18\},\\
--   D(n,R,I)&\le20S^3.
--   \end{aligned}
--   $$
--   This uniformly bounds the additional call depth needed by the stage from the scheduled dimensions and its incidence capacity. It is one component of the selected-color program's finite resource requirements.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/EncodedColorWantedResources.lean#L128-L142

